course: dictionary
lesson: 9757
title: Supple: bending with ease
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Supple means able to bend and move easily. A supple body can twist and stretch without strain, like a gymnast's. «Stretching keeps muscles supple.» The sentence tells you that stretching helps muscles stay easy to bend.
explain: Supple can also describe materials that bend without cracking, such as leather or a willow twig. «The supple willow branches bend over the river.» The branches bend over the water instead of snapping, so supple must mean bendy, not stiff.
explain: Use the swap test. Put bendy in place of supple: «The dancer is bendy» still makes sense, so bendy is a good meaning for supple.
fact: Supple means able to bend and move easily.
fact: Supple can also mean soft and bending without cracking, like supple leather.
fact: The comparison forms are suppler (more bendy) and supplest (the most bendy).
fact: «Gymnasts and dancers are very supple.»
fact: Supple is an old word that is still used in English today.
exercise: «The supple willow branches bend over the river.» What does supple mean here? | Wet and muddy | Loud and rustling | Stiff and straight | *Bendy, able to bend without snapping
exercise: Gymnasts are very ___. Which word fits best? | Hungry | Noisy | *Supple | Sleepy
exercise: What does «supple leather» mean? | *Soft and able to bend without cracking | Very heavy and hard | Shiny and brand new | Dirty and cracked
test: «Stretching keeps muscles supple.» What does supple mean here? | Sore and tired | *Able to bend and move easily | Hard and stiff | Very strong
test: Which material is supple, able to bend without cracking? | Glass | Iron | Rock | *Rubber
exam: Which sentence uses supple correctly to mean bendy? | *The dancer was so supple she could touch her toes | The loud bell was supple | The old wooden table was supple and strong | The cold ice was supple
